# SmartIQ_PDP site settings. On the server this file lives in the PARAMS
# branch, not beside the scripts:
#
#   cp smartiq.env.example /datalakebin/prod/gold/integration/params/membership/smartiq_pdp/smartiq.env
#   chmod 600 .../params/membership/smartiq_pdp/smartiq.env
#
# Because it is not beside the launcher, EVERY invocation (interactive or
# Control-M) must export its location first:
#
#   export SMARTIQ_ENV_FILE=/datalakebin/prod/gold/integration/params/membership/smartiq_pdp/smartiq.env
#
# smartiq.env is gitignored: it holds site values, not framework
# configuration. Everything about HOW the feed behaves lives in the .conf
# files; only WHERE it runs lives here.

# ---- SQL Server -------------------------------------------------------------
# LOWER-ENVIRONMENT values. Production promotion swaps these for the prod
# host/database/account (PROD_PROMOTION.md Phase 1) — nothing else changes.
SMARTIQ_HOST=dwauswbasq01.adhcscdev.net
SMARTIQ_PORT=1433
SMARTIQ_DB=DLM
SMARTIQ_USER=svc_ingest

# The source table is NOT set here — run_smartiq.sh derives it from the
# environment you select (e2e or prod) so the two cannot be crossed.

# ---- Password ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave this UNSET. The launcher prompts without echoing, which keeps the
# value out of shell history, out of `ps`, and out of this file.
#
# CLUSTER MODE EXPOSES IT REGARDLESS. The driver runs in a YARN container and
# the `env` password provider reads that container's environment, so the value
# must be forwarded as spark.yarn.appMasterEnv — which places it in the
# spark-submit command line, readable by `ps` on this host and visible in the
# YARN launch context. Verified, not assumed: client mode keeps it out of argv,
# cluster mode does not. That is a property of the env provider, not of this
# launcher.
#
# Tolerable for a lower-environment service account. For production, switch the
# feed's password provider to cyberark / azure_keyvault / conjur — the driver
# then fetches the credential under its own identity and nothing passes through
# the shell or the command line at all.
#
# For unattended runs (Control-M), the job command reads it from the
# 400-permission secret file in params (value never appears in the command
# text or sysout):
#
#   export SMARTIQ_DB_PASSWORD="$(cat /datalakebin/prod/gold/integration/params/membership/smartiq_pdp/smartiq.pwd)"
#
# SMARTIQ_DB_PASSWORD=

# ---- Site paths (DEPLOYMENT.md "Site layout") --------------------------------
# Directory holding feed-*.conf and its included *-schema.conf, side by side.
SMARTIQ_CONF_DIR=/datalakebin/prod/gold/integration/params/membership/smartiq_pdp

# Assembly jar built from main.
SMARTIQ_JAR=/datalakebin/prod/gold/integration/bin/membership/smartiq_pdp/ingestion-app-1.0.0-SNAPSHOT-jar-with-dependencies.jar

# Microsoft JDBC driver — use the jre11 build to match Java 11.
SMARTIQ_JDBC_DRIVER=/datalakebin/prod/gold/integration/bin/membership/smartiq_pdp/mssql-jdbc-12.4.2.jre11.jar

# ---- Submit -----------------------------------------------------------------
# client  = driver runs here; env inherited; logs on your terminal.
# cluster = driver runs in a YARN container; what Control-M uses.
SMARTIQ_DEPLOY_MODE=client

# Driver heap. The 364-column feed builds a large analyzer plan BEFORE
# reading any row, and the cluster default was not enough. Leave unset for
# the 11-column lower-env feed.
INGEST_DRIVER_MEMORY=4g

# ---- Alerting ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The feed configs reference ${?SMARTIQ_ALERT_WEBHOOK}, so the endpoint lives
# here rather than in a file under version control. Unset = the placeholder in
# the feed applies and delivery simply fails (logged, run unaffected).
#SMARTIQ_ALERT_WEBHOOK=https://hooks.example.com/services/XXXX

# ---- Load-type label --------------------------------------------------------
# Stamped on every RAW row as file_type, derived from the run mode, so a full
# load and an incremental are distinguishable in the data itself. Override the
# labels here if your convention differs; pass --raw-flag explicitly to
# override a single run.
#
# Deliberately NOT a partition key: RAW retention drops partitions on a
# single-key ingest_dt layout only, so adding a second key would disable
# purging, and a two-value column prunes almost nothing.
#SMARTIQ_RAW_FLAG_FULL=F
#SMARTIQ_RAW_FLAG_INCR=I

# ---- Operational override (optional) ----------------------------------------
# A second config whose values WIN over the feed config, for changes that
# cannot wait for a change order — a longer lock lease during an incident, a
# temporarily relaxed reject threshold, a different alert endpoint.
#
#   feeds.smartiq_pdp.concurrency.lease_minutes = 120
#
# Objects merge, lists are replaced. Every overridden path is logged by name;
# the run ledger marks the run with an "+ovr:" fingerprint suffix. A path set
# here but missing on disk FAILS the run (CFG_019) rather than applying
# silently. Remove it once the real change is deployed.
#INGEST_OVERRIDE_FILE=/datalakebin/prod/gold/integration/params/membership/smartiq_pdp/override-smartiq-pdp.conf
